From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taran9999 <tdwivedu@cisco.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: adj: honour ethernet-output features on L2 (VNET_LINK_ETHERNET)
 adjacencies

adj_l2_rewrite_inline() already dispatches the ethernet-output feature
arc for an L2 rewrite/midchain, but only when the adjacency carries
VNET_REWRITE_HAS_FEATURES. Nothing ever sets that flag for a
VNET_LINK_ETHERNET adjacency: both the creation-time evaluator
(adj_nbr_evaluate_feature) and the feature-toggle walk
(adj_feature_update_walk_cb) only map the ip4/ip6/mpls output arcs onto
their matching link types and bail on everything else.

As a result an ethernet-output feature enabled on an L2 interface (e.g.
a GRE TEB tunnel used by SONiC Everflow, whose midchain adjacency is
VNET_LINK_ETHERNET and stacks on the IPv4 underlay) is listed by
"show interface features" yet never runs, because the tunnel's adjacency
takes the plain rewrite_header.next_index path and skips the arc.

Add the ethernet-output arc / VNET_LINK_ETHERNET case to both places so
the flag tracks ethernet-output features the same way it already tracks
the L3 arcs. The flag is still only set when feature_count > 0, so
interfaces with no ethernet-output feature are unaffected.

Also register adj-l2-rewrite as a start node of the ethernet-output arc.
adj_l2_rewrite_inline() is shared by adj-l2-midchain and adj-l2-rewrite
and starts the arc from either one, but only adj-l2-midchain was declared
as a start node, so vnet_config add_next() never created the edge from
adj-l2-rewrite to the first feature node and adj-l2-rewrite (registered
with n_next_nodes = 1) would enqueue to an out-of-range next index. Before
this patch nothing set HAS_FEATURES on an ETHERNET adjacency so that path
was unreachable; a plain (non-midchain) L2 adjacency uses adj-l2-rewrite
per adj_get_rewrite_node(), so the arc must start there too.
---
 src/vnet/adj/adj.c        | 5 ++++-
 src/vnet/adj/adj_nbr.c    | 5 +++++
 src/vnet/ethernet/init.c  | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vnet/adj/adj.c b/src/vnet/adj/adj.c
index 37ad4654f..2dd0922d5 100644
--- a/src/vnet/adj/adj.c
+++ b/src/vnet/adj/adj.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <vnet/adj/adj_delegate.h>
 #include <vnet/fib/fib_node_list.h>
 #include <vnet/fib/fib_walk.h>
+#include <vnet/ethernet/ethernet.h>
 
 /* Adjacency packet/byte counters indexed by adjacency index. */
 vlib_combined_counter_main_t adjacency_counters = {
@@ -420,7 +421,9 @@ adj_feature_update_walk_cb (adj_index_t ai,
         ((ctx->arc == ip4_main.lookup_main.output_feature_arc_index) &&
          (VNET_LINK_IP4 == adj->ia_link)) ||
         ((ctx->arc == mpls_main.output_feature_arc_index) &&
-         (VNET_LINK_MPLS == adj->ia_link)))
+         (VNET_LINK_MPLS == adj->ia_link)) ||
+        ((ctx->arc == ethernet_main.output_feature_arc_index) &&
+         (VNET_LINK_ETHERNET == adj->ia_link)))
     {
         vnet_feature_main_t *fm = &feature_main;
         vnet_feature_config_main_t *cm;
diff --git a/src/vnet/adj/adj_nbr.c b/src/vnet/adj/adj_nbr.c
index df33ec504..f508cd70d 100644
--- a/src/vnet/adj/adj_nbr.c
+++ b/src/vnet/adj/adj_nbr.c
@@ -200,6 +200,11 @@ adj_nbr_evaluate_feature (adj_index_t ai)
     case VNET_LINK_MPLS:
         arc_index = mpls_main.output_feature_arc_index;
         break;
+    case VNET_LINK_ETHERNET:
+        /* L2 (e.g. GRE TEB) midchain rewrite dispatches the ethernet-output
+         * arc in adj_l2_rewrite_inline() but only honours HAS_FEATURES. */
+        arc_index = ethernet_main.output_feature_arc_index;
+        break;
     default:
         return;
     }
diff --git a/src/vnet/ethernet/init.c b/src/vnet/ethernet/init.c
index 000000000..000000000 100644
--- a/src/vnet/ethernet/init.c
+++ b/src/vnet/ethernet/init.c
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ VNET_FEATURE_ARC_INIT (ethernet_output, static) =
 {
   .arc_name  = "ethernet-output",
   .last_in_arc = "error-drop",
-  .start_nodes = VNET_FEATURES ("adj-l2-midchain"),
+  .start_nodes = VNET_FEATURES ("adj-l2-midchain", "adj-l2-rewrite"),
   .arc_index_ptr = &ethernet_main.output_feature_arc_index,
 };
 
